---
import SEO from '../components/SEO.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<!doctype html>

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<SEO
			title="CIO Book | How to Become CIO and Succeed"
			description="How to Become CIO and Succeed is a practical CIO book about leadership, people, business, strategy, and creating value through technology."
			lang="en"
		/>
	</head>

	<body>
		<Header />

		<main>
			<section class="hero">
				<p class="books-page-label">
					A Practical CIO Book
				</p>

				<h1>
					How to Become <span class="accent">CIO</span><br />
					and Succeed
				</h1>

				<div class="lead-principles">
					<div>People First</div>
					<div>Business Driven</div>
					<div>Technology Enabled</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="book">
				<article
					class="books-page-book books-page-book-featured"
					aria-labelledby="cio-book-title"
				>
					<div class="books-page-cover-wrapper">
						<img
							src="/images/cio-book-cover.jpg"
							alt="Cover of the CIO book How to Become CIO and Succeed by Fede Rodrigo"
							class="books-page-cover"
						/>
					</div>

					<div class="books-page-content">
						<p class="books-page-label">
							CIO Leadership Book
						</p>

						<h2 id="cio-book-title">
							Technology is Never the Starting Point
						</h2>

						<p class="books-page-subtitle">
							People, Business, Strategy
						</p>

						<p>
							The CIO role is not about managing systems. It is about
							leading people, understanding the business, shaping
							strategy, influencing decisions, and turning technology
							into a competitive advantage
						</p>

						<p>
							<em>How to Become CIO and Succeed</em> is a practical CIO
							book for technology professionals who want to become
							business leaders, as well as current CIOs seeking to
							strengthen their leadership and increase their impact
						</p>

						<p>
							This is the book I wish I had when I began my own
							leadership journey.
						</p>

						<p class="books-page-action">
							<a
								href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F8MVPN4Q"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener noreferrer"
							>
								Buy the book on Amazon →
							</a>
						</p>
					</div>
				</article>
			</section>

			<section id="about-the-book" class="contact-section">
				<h2>About the Book</h2>

				<div class="about-content">
					<p>
						Many technology professionals believe that becoming a CIO
						depends primarily on technical expertise. Technical knowledge
						matters, but it is not enough
					</p>

					<p>
						A successful Chief Information Officer must understand how
						the organization creates value, build strong relationships,
						develop capable teams, communicate clearly, make difficult
						decisions, and connect technology with business priorities
					</p>

					<p>
						This book explores the practical lessons behind that
						transition: from managing technology to leading through
						technology
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="what-you-will-learn" class="contact-section">
				<h2>What You Will Learn</h2>

				<div class="about-content">
					<p>
						You will learn how to move beyond the traditional view of IT
						and become a trusted business leader
					</p>

					<p>
						The book examines how CIOs can build effective teams, create
						a service-oriented culture, earn credibility, influence
						executive decisions, improve operations, shape technology
						strategy, and consistently create business value
					</p>

					<p>
						It does not present a rigid formula. It offers practical
						principles developed through more than 25 years of technology
						and leadership experience
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="who-is-this-book-for" class="contact-section">
				<h2>Who This CIO Book Is For</h2>

				<div class="about-content">
					<p>
						<em>How to Become CIO and Succeed</em> is written for IT
						managers, technology directors, aspiring CIOs, current Chief
						Information Officers, and technology leaders who want to
						create a greater impact within their organizations.
					</p>

					<p>
						It is also relevant for business executives who want to
						better understand the role a modern CIO should play
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

		

			<section id="buy" class="contact-section">
				<h2>Get the Book</h2>

				<div class="about-content">
					<p>
						Discover a practical approach to CIO leadership built around
						people, business, strategy, and technology.
					</p>

					<p class="books-page-action">
						<a
							href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F8MVPN4Q"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
						>
							Buy How to Become CIO and Succeed →
						</a>
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
